<title>ESTONIA: MEAT PROCESSORS PROTEST TARIFF PROPOSAL - REPORT.</title>
<headline>MEAT PROCESSORS PROTEST TARIFF PROPOSAL - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Meat Producers Association plans to submit a statement on Tuesday to Economics Minister Jaak Leimann rejecting the planned introduction of tariffs on pork imports, Aripaev newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The group, representing meat processors in Estonia, said the planned tariff would mean a 17 percent rise in the cost of pork products and a decrease in sales, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The statement also said pork production will decrease and the move will reduce the competitiveness of local producers on international markets.</p>
<p>The chief executives of the companies said the planned tariff could harm Estonia's positive image abroad, the newspaper quoted them as adding.</p>
<p>The meat producers association includes the free market listed Rakvere meat plant .</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
